<title>RWANDA: Zaire rebels say near camp, took part of town.</title>
<headline>Zaire rebels say near camp, took part of town.</headline>
<dateline>KIGALI 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rebels said on Friday they were six km (four miles) from the largest refugee camp in eastern Zaire but were delaying an advance for the sake of innocent refugees there.</p>
<p>Mwenze Kongoro, minister of justice in rebel leader Laurent Kabila's administration in east Zaire, told Reuters rebel forces had seized one side of Kindu town and were taking the other.</p>
